      "name": "draw_mline",
      "description": "Draw a multiline (MLINE) through the given vertices using a named multiline style - the way a wall of a defined type is drawn in one call rather than as two offset polylines that must be kept parallel by hand. style defaults to the drawing\u0027s current one; create one first with create_mlinestyle. justification is \u0027top\u0027, \u0027zero\u0027 or \u0027bottom\u0027 and decides which of the style\u0027s parallel lines the vertices you pass actually lie on, so it changes where the wall sits relative to your points. scale multiplies every element offset, so a 200mm style drawn at scale 1.5 is 300mm wide.",
